# GitHub API rate-limit throttle

Any agent flow that shells out to `gh` — PR / issue triage, review replies,
CI polling, `gh api`, and `gh pr` / `gh issue` reads and writes — must run it as:

```
"${REPOSITORY_HELPERS_DIR:-$HOME/work/ai/repository-helpers}/scripts/gh-api" <gh args…>
```

so GitHub **primary and secondary** rate-limit backoff is automatic — the same
`github_api_exec_with_rate_limit_retry` logic `wait-for-agent-review` and
`github-repo-lint` already use internally. A direct `gh` call 403s hard for the
better part of an hour once GitHub's *secondary* limiter trips.

Args, stdin, stdout, and the exit code (including `125` for quota-intact
fail-fast) pass straight through. Interactive `gh` (`auth`, prompts, `--web`) is
exempt; `scripts/gh-api -- <args>` opts in a subcommand the wrapper rejects.

